.TH HULL-GUI 1 "2026-11-26" "hull 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hull-gui, hull-tui \- manage hull's machines from one window, on the desktop or a terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hull-gui
.RB [ \-\-hull
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-tui | \-\-gui ]
.RI [ FILE ...]
.br
.B hull-tui
.RI [ FILE ...]
.br
.B hull-gui \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hull-gui
lists the machines added to it, those in folders of their own in
.IR ~/hull ,
and those hull's core is running, and starts, stops, saves, pauses and watches
them: their plan, their output, their resources and their networks, a
machine's terminal, and its screen in a tab beside them or a window of its
own. New writes a machine into
.IR ~/hull/NAME ,
a PC with a new disk and its installer disc among them;
Import copies a VirtualBox or VMware machine or an appliance there, its
disks converted; Export Appliance writes one as an .ova that VirtualBox
and VMware import; Settings edits its hardware, disks and discs in its
.I hull.conf
in place, writing only what changed; Snapshots keeps a stopped PC's
disks to go back to; Clone copies one; Remove takes one
off the list or deletes its folder to the desktop's trash.
.PP
.B hull-tui
is the same window drawn on the terminal. Each
.I FILE
given is a
.I hull.conf
or another hypervisor's machine file added to the list.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-hull " PATH"
the hull to run machines with; by default the one beside hull-gui, else
hull on the PATH.
.TP
.B \-\-tui
draw on the terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-gui
draw on the desktop.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HULL_THEME
.B dark
or
.B light
overrides the desktop's own scheme.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hull (1)
